<title>BELGIUM: Farm ministers delay pesticides decision.</title>
<headline>Farm ministers delay pesticides decision.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union farm ministers on Tuesday sent a Commission proposal to harmonise pesticide residues in food back to a committee of national experts, a German official said.</p>
<p>&quot;Ministers agreed to a German request, backed by Denmark and Sweden, that the proposal should exempt baby food because standards are higher in those countries,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The Commission proposal, which will now be considered by COREPER, seeks to harmonise levels of pesticide residues in food and would amend four existing directives.</p>
</text>
